A while ago, I wrote a patch which rigs NetHack's random number 
generator so that two players will go through the same dungeon and have 
mostly the same things happen to them. Not much has been done with it 
so far (it was written too late to use in last year's tournament), so I 
put some thought into how a Duplicate NetHack tournament would work.

Because everyone's playing through the same dungeon, players can't play 
many games. So rather than doing the tournament once a year, it would 
be done as a regular event - say, once a week.

- At the start of the week (preferrably on a Friday), a random seed is 
  chosen.
- All games are played on a public server. Players can start playing at 
  any time for the next 7 days.
- Each player can only play one game per tournament. If you die, you 
  have to wait for the next one.
- Players are allowed to read and take advantage of information in 
  post-mortems, YAAPs, and so on that get posted to the newsgroup.
- All games must be finished within two weeks of the start of the
  tournament.
- The fastest ascenscion wins. If no one ascends, high score wins.
  (Interesting alternative: best conduct ascenscion wins instead.)

Players who start early will have more time to finish. Players who 
start late will get more warning of what the dungeon has in store for 
them. (I figure that's better and easier than trying to stop people 
from trading notes. Item descriptions are still randomized.)

Unfortunately, I can't host tournaments myself. But if people agree 
that it's a good idea, it'd be cool if one of the public NetHack 
servers could host it.

